,87,61,20,488,220,22,87,61,19,481,220,17,284,220,15,2418,220,7379,198,59,7265,90,6612,9,532,5,59,37018,90,64,61,19,15170,7,64,481,293,2376,64,481,272,2376,64,481,294,2376,64,481,384,9139,488,1124,37018,90,65,61,19,15170,7,65,481,264,2376,65,481,272,2376,65,481,294,2376,65,481,384,9139,90155,5,59,31610,488,1124,37018,90,66,61,19,15170,7,66,481,264,2376,66,481,293,2376,66,481,294,2376,66,481,384,9139,488,1124,37018,90,67,61,19,15170,7,67,481,264,2376,67,481,293,2376,67,481,272,2376,67,481,384,9139,90155,5,59,31610,488,1124,37018,90,68,61,19,15170,7,68,481,264,2376,68,481,293,2376,68,481,272,2376,68,481,294,9139,624,59,408,90,6612,9,92,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ $d,$ and $e$ be the distinct roots of the equation $x^5 + 7x^4 - 2 = 0.$  Find\n\\begin{align*}\n&\\frac{a^4}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} + \\frac{b^4}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)} \\\\\n&\\quad + \\frac{c^4}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)} + \\frac{d^4}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)} \\\\\n&\\quad + \\frac{e^4}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)}.\n\\end{align*}","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"175283ef9db316cebac0e7ac39fac6f9f931df72facfd7e88e41c3ee8220735e"},"seconds":29.444535493850708,"seed":206074769744230114,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the given problem, we start by noting that \\(a, b, c, d, e\\) are the distinct roots of the polynomial \\(P(x) = x^5 + 7x^4 - 2 = 0\\). We need to evaluate the expression:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a^4}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} + \\frac{b^4}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)} + \\frac{c^4}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)} + \\frac{d^4}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)} + \\frac{e^4}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)}\n\\]\n\nThis expression is a form of Lagrange interpolation for the polynomial \\(Q(x) = x^4\\). Specifically, it can be written as:\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{i=0}^{4} \\frac{P_i(a_i) \\cdot a_i^4}{\\prod_{j \\neq i} (a_i - a_j)}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(P_i(x)\\) is the Lagrange basis polynomial given by:\n\n\\[\nP_i(x) = \\prod_{\\substack{1 \\le j \\le 5 \\\\ j \\neq i}} \\frac{x - a_j}{a_i - a_j}\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the sum of \\(P_i(a_i) \\cdot a_i^4\\). Notice that:\n\n\\[\nP_i(a_i) = \\prod_{\\substack{1 \\le j \\le 5 \\\\ j \\neq i}} \\frac{a_i - a_j}{a_i - a_j} = 1\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{i=0}^{4} \\frac{a_i^4}{\\prod_{j \\neq i} (a_i - a_j)}\n\\]\n\nThis is the value of the polynomial \\(Q(x) = x^4\\) evaluated at the roots of \\(P(x)\\) using the Lagrange interpolation formula. Therefore, we need to evaluate:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a^4 + b^4 + c^4 + d^4 + e^4}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e) + (b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e) + (c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e) + (d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e) + (e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)}\n\\]\n\nThe denominator is the value of the polynomial \\(\\prod_{i=1}^5 (x - a_i)\\) evaluated at \\(x = a_i\\) for each \\(i\\), which is \\((-1)^5 P(a_i) = -P(a_i)\\). Summing these values over all \\(i\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{i=1}^5 (-P(a_i)) = -\\left( P(a) + P(b) + P(c) + P(d) + P(e) \\right)\n\\]\n\nSince \\(a, b, c, d, e\\) are roots of \\(P(x) = x^5 + 7x^4 - 2\\), we have \\(P(a) = P(b) = P(c) = P(d) = P(e) = 0\\). Therefore, the sum is:\n\n\\[\n-\\left(0 + 0 + 0 + 0 + 0\\right) = 0\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a^4 + b^4 + c^4 + d^4 + e^4}{0}\n\\]\n\nHowever, the correct interpretation is that the sum of the Lagrange interpolation terms for \\(Q(x) = x^4\\) is simply the value of \\(Q(x)\\) evaluated at the roots of \\(P(x)\\), which is:\n\n\\[\na^4 + b^4 + c^4 + d^4 + e^4\n\\]\n\nGiven that \\(P(x) = x^5 + 7x^4 - 2\\) and the sum of the fourth powers of the roots of a polynomial \\(x^5 + 7x^4 + \\cdots\\) can be found using symmetric sums, we use Newton's sums. Let \\(S_k = a^k + b^k + c^k + d^k + e^k\\). From the polynomial, we have:\n\n\\[\nS_1 = -7, \\quad S_2 = 49 - 2S_1 = 49 + 14 = 63, \\quad S_3 = -7S_2 + 2S_1 = -441 - 14 = -455\n\\]\n\nUsing the recurrence relation for symmetric sums:\n\n\\[\nS_4 = -7S_3 + 2S_2 = -7(-455) + 2(63) = 3185 + 126 = 3311\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the given expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3311}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{3311}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"intermediate_algebra:153"}
